# One edit reaching every machine: announce, then fetch (SPEC §6)
shape: sequence_diagram

user: you edit ~/notes/todo.md on A
wa: A watcher
a: A engine
b: B engine
c: C engine

user -> wa: save (editors write in bursts)
wa -> a: path changed (after 200 ms of quiet)
a -> a: "hash it; same as current? stop (this is also how echoes stop)"
a -> a: "new version: vector[A]+1, parent = previous"
a -> b: "ANNOUNCE {path, hash, vector, mtime}"
b -> b: "compare vectors: newer → fetch\nolder/equal → ignore\nconcurrent → fetch, then resolve (diagram 04)"
b -> a: FETCH path
a -> b: "FILE {version, ancestry, content}"
b -> b: "apply: temp file, fsync, re-check the target, rename"
b -> c: "ANNOUNCE (passed on, never back to A)"
c -> b: FETCH
b -> c: FILE
c -> c: apply
a -> c: "ANNOUNCE (if A–C is up too)"
c -> c: "already have it: equal vector, ignore"
